(4153674, 594002, 70000, '<td valign="top">Wow I cannot believe people....only two comments? The detail in this one is just unbelievable and the position of the spider works perfectly in the composition. I agree that it fitting the challenge can be questioned but as a photograph you have taken a classic pretty flower picture and turned it into something more. I gave this a nine. Fabulous shot</td>', 'Wow I cannot believe people....only two comments? The detail in this one is just unbelievable and the position of the spider works perfectly in the composition. I agree that it fitting the challenge can be questioned but as a photograph you have taken a classic pretty flower picture and turned it into something more. I gave this a nine. Fabulous shot', '2007-10-09 03:02:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4153683, 593307, 66384, '<td valign="top">This shot has so much potential. The focus and exposure are great. I love the nice relaxed expression you captured. I like the crop too. I hope you won''t mind my sharing a few ideas of what I would like to do with it. <br/> <br/>In an extreme close up of a girl this age, I would do a significant amount of retouching. I find the darkness and texture around the nose, and the specks on the lips distracting. I would use the healing brush to clear up any blemishes, and a very slight surface blur to smooth any roughness in the skin. I would also remove the hair covering her eyebrow. The eye is a beautiful feature, and I think it could be enhanced by slightly burning the edge of the eyelashes like eyeliner. The white of the eye almost looks painted. I might use the healing brush to remove the worst of the red lines, but I''d leave enough detail to keep it real.<br/> <br/>I don''t know if these "enhancements" would make it a better photo, but I think the girl would enjoy it more.</td>', 'This shot has so much potential. The focus and exposure are great. I love the nice relaxed expression you captured. I like the crop too. I hope you won''t mind my sharing a few ideas of what I would like to do with it.  In an extreme close up of a girl this age, I would do a significant amount of retouching. I find the darkness and texture around the nose, and the specks on the lips distracting. I would use the healing brush to clear up any blemishes, and a very slight surface blur to smooth any roughness in the skin. I would also remove the hair covering her eyebrow. The eye is a beautiful feature, and I think it could be enhanced by slightly burning the edge of the eyelashes like eyeliner. The white of the eye almost looks painted. I might use the healing brush to remove the worst of the red lines, but I''d leave enough detail to keep it real. I don''t know if these "enhancements" would make it a better photo, but I think the girl would enjoy it more.', '2007-10-09 03:09:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4153688, 592438, 30982, '<td valign="top">He''s got his dad''s sneer, doesn''t he?  Post the whole thing so we can fully appreciate that sneer.</td>', 'He''s got his dad''s sneer, doesn''t he?  Post the whole thing so we can fully appreciate that sneer.', '2007-10-09 03:19:01.000000', NULL, 0),
