(4185159, 593952, 61651, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a TSer too, but thought it was raish. :)  Stepping outside your comfort zone is a good thing - glad you had such a great time with this, seems like the possibilities are endless with a prop like this one.</td>', 'I thought this was a TSer too, but thought it was raish. :)  Stepping outside your comfort zone is a good thing - glad you had such a great time with this, seems like the possibilities are endless with a prop like this one.', '2007-10-21 15:39:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4185163, 593577, 61651, '<td valign="top">The grainy, colored pencil-sketch look works well for this shot - a fine take on the challenge, and unfairly punished in the voting.</td>', 'The grainy, colored pencil-sketch look works well for this shot - a fine take on the challenge, and unfairly punished in the voting.', '2007-10-21 15:41:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4185170, 593789, 61651, '<td valign="top">It''s a pain to shoot reflective surfaces and not get yourself in the shot. :)  I just read the other day to point the lens through a hole in a large panel of cloth (black or white, depending on the reflection you''re looking for) to disguise the camera and surroundings - I offer that tip to you, should you find it useful, although I haven''t made use of it myself, yet, to know how well it works.  I like the simple directness of the shot, and the focus, although I had assumed it was at a wider aperture.  I''m surprised that at f/8 you didn''t get more of the rim of the lens in focus. I like how you focused it, as I said, I just assumed it was at a different aperture.</td>', 'It''s a pain to shoot reflective surfaces and not get yourself in the shot. :)  I just read the other day to point the lens through a hole in a large panel of cloth (black or white, depending on the reflection you''re looking for) to disguise the camera and surroundings - I offer that tip to you, should you find it useful, although I haven''t made use of it myself, yet, to know how well it works.  I like the simple directness of the shot, and the focus, although I had assumed it was at a wider aperture.  I''m surprised that at f/8 you didn''t get more of the rim of the lens in focus. I like how you focused it, as I said, I just assumed it was at a different aperture.', '2007-10-21 15:47:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4185172, 591599, 61651, '<td valign="top">Two "halfs" for the price of one - I think this is quite a poignant shot.</td>', 'Two "halfs" for the price of one - I think this is quite a poignant shot.', '2007-10-21 15:48:15.000000', NULL, 0),
